# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/exact-end window (exact resume P0 on the production stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/exact-end and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-xe-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-xe-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory, in the prefix gate's
# containers too (c2_prefix_gate.py reads every arm's log for the checkpoint lines and fails the arm without them); the keys are the same in every serving job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# XL1 (TIMED, the ARM of the first returning-turn ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-xe, the approved ship-4 profile with the gate marker in
# place of its owner waiver id, the undrop and the window carry, the same plan and conversations as XC1, on Swift. READ after the four boots of the pair (XC1 XL1 XC2 XL2):
# python3 scripts/ci/exact_resume_compare.py <XC1 results>/prefix/exact-resume-timed <XL1 ...> and the same for (XC2, XL2): every paired hit IDENTICAL across the arms (both
# are exact against their cold twins, so the same messages give the same answers), the lever's Q at floor2048(P) or above where the control's is floor2048(P) - 2048, and
# the TTFT delta per conversation (~9k, ~33k, ~120k). ESTIMATE to beat (docs/tp4-exact-end.md 4, modelled from the card medians): about -0.9 s of 2.1 s at 165k for the
# typical returning turn (two 2048-row forwards become one); a pair whose delta is not negative beyond the control-to-control spread (XC1 against XC2) is no gain. GO needs
# both pairs negative beyond the spread and the texts equal. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job
# beside it. the carry's lines: "[PINDIAG] prefix: window carry engaged undrop=1 carry=1" once, "... carried req= Q= P= rows=" for every carried admission and "... stored
# req= pos= rows= bytes= ms=" for every export, and, beside the tile-aligned window of this profile, "[PINDIAG] tap window aligned engaged ... parts=2" on a carried turn
# (the carried rows are the first aligned part: prefix_window_carry.Carried.align) with no "fell back" line CHECKPOINT READ (the prefix gate checks every arm's container
# log, the smoke step passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the arm's
# result line says "checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a: read". Duration (estimate): 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-xe-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exact-resume-timed
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-xe
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
